      },
      "worked": "Let $f(x)=e^x-2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=e^x-2\\\\f'(\\ln 3)&=e^{\\ln 3}-2\\\\f'(\\ln 3)&=1\\\\f(\\ln 3)&=e^{\\ln 3}-2\\ln 3\\\\f(\\ln 3)&=3-2\\ln 3\\end{align*}$$\nThe point is $(\\ln 3,3-2\\ln 3)$ and the tangent gradient is $m_T=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}m_N&=-\\frac{1}{m_T}\\\\m_N&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the point-gradient formula, the tangent is\n$$\\begin{align*}y-(3-2\\ln 3)&=1(x-\\ln 3)\\\\y&=x+3-3\\ln 3\\end{align*}$$\nThe normal is\n$$\\begin{align*}y-(3-2\\ln 3)&=-1(x-\\ln 3)\\\\y&=-x+3-\\ln 3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
